=== s1: grid-and-reach agreement ===
s1: grid-and-reach agreement between vocabulary A and vocabulary B
box: W in [0,10], F in [0,10]  ->  121 numerals

Q1 set equality      : 121/121

Q2 08's predicate over a discriminating pool (accepts AND rejects):
    ok  fixed W=4 F=2                        got accept  want accept  
    ok  fixed W=8 F=0                        got accept  want accept  
    ok  fixed W=1 F=4                        got accept  want accept  
    ok  fixed W=0 F=0                        got accept  want accept  
    ok  fixed W=6 F=6                        got accept  want accept  
    ok  HUB W=4 F=2 (phase half a step)      got reject  want reject  binade -3: 1/8 is not on the step lattice
    ok  float p=4 e=-3..3                    got reject  want reject  binade -2: step 1/32, expected 1/64
    ok  decimal 2 digits F10=1               got reject  want reject  step 1/10 is not a power of radix 2
    ok  ragged progression                   got reject  want reject  binade 0: 2 distinct steps [Fraction(1, 4), Fraction(1, 2)]
    ok  fixed W=4 F=2, wrong step asserted   got reject  want reject  binade -1: step 1/4, expected 1/8
    -> 10/10 verdicts correct

I = W - F as the binade the reach stops at (exclusive):
  W=4   F=0   I=4    reach=[0,2^4) = [0,16)   max value 15
  W=4   F=2   I=2    reach=[0,2^2) = [0,4)   max value 15/4
  W=4   F=4   I=0    reach=[0,2^0) = [0,1)   max value 15/16
  W=1   F=1   I=0    reach=[0,2^0) = [0,1)   max value 1/2
  W=1   F=8   I=-7   reach=[0,2^-7) = [0,1/128)   max value 1/256
  W=1   F=32  I=-31  reach=[0,2^-31) = [0,1/2147483648)   max value 1/4294967296
  W=0   F=0   I=0    reach=[0,2^0) = [0,1)   max value 0

negative I is the reach lying wholly below one, which needs no signed storage:
  W=1 F=1: I=0, values are exactly {0, 2^-1}, one bit
  W=1 F=2: I=-1, values are exactly {0, 2^-2}, one bit
  W=1 F=4: I=-3, values are exactly {0, 2^-4}, one bit
  W=1 F=8: I=-7, values are exactly {0, 2^-8}, one bit
  W=1 F=32: I=-31, values are exactly {0, 2^-32}, one bit

=== s2: which numerals the width keying misses ===
s2: which A-numerals admit a (W, F) presentation

representation                       A-shape                    (W,F)?   detail
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fixed point W=4 F=2                  constant f                 YES      W=4 F=2  |V|=16
fixed point W=8 F=8                  constant f                 YES      W=8 F=8  |V|=256
zero-only numeral W=0                constant f                 YES      W=0 F=0  |V|=1
negative derived I: W=1 F=4          constant f                 YES      W=1 F=4  |V|=2
HUB W=4 F=2 (phase half a step)      constant f, phase 1/2      NO       does not start at zero (min is 1/8)
Ranged, 12 values at F=2             constant f, count not 2^k  NO       cardinality 12 is not a power of two
Ranged, 100 values at F=0            constant f, count not 2^k  NO       cardinality 100 is not a power of two
float p=4 emin=-3 emax=3             f slope one                NO       7 distinct steps, not one progression
float p=3 emin=-2 emax=2             f slope one                NO       5 distinct steps, not one progression
float+subnormals p=4 e=-3..3         f knee then slope one      NO       7 distinct steps, not one progression
posit-shaped, f slope two            f slope two                NO       12 distinct steps, not one progression
decimal 2 digits, F10=1              radix ten                  NO       step 1/10 denominator is not a power of two
bias = 1/2, W=4 F=2                  bias non-zero              NO       does not start at zero (min is 1/2)
adjustment = 3, W=4 F=2              adjustment not one         NO       step 3/4 is not a negative power of two (numerator 3)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
presentable: 4/14    not presentable: 10/14

Every case above is INSIDE 08's format concept (08:303-331). So the misses are
numerals the concept admits and the (W, F) keying cannot name.

grouped by which A coordinate the (W, F) pair does not carry:
  canonical exponent not constant : float, float+subnormals, posit-shaped
  phase not zero                  : HUB
  radix not two                   : decimal
  bias not zero                   : bias = 1/2
  adjustment not one              : adjustment = 3
  reach not a power of the radix   : Ranged (both rows)

